WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:08.120
Hi everyone, welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners, Episode 31 for May 7th, 2026.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.220
Let's break down today's coolest AI news so anyone can understand it.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:18.420
Some awesome AI developments today, and we're going to make all of it make sense.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.240
Let's get into it.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:26.420
So picture this, you open your laptop to work on a school project, and instead of switching

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.500
between tabs and apps yourself, a helpful assistant just sits beside you and does the

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.260
clicking for you.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.140
That is basically what perplexity just made possible for every Mac user.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.480
Their personal computer AI assistant is now available to anyone with a Mac.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.420
No paid subscription needed.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:51.040
Before today it was only for people who paid for a higher plan, but now it is open to all.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:56.100
Think of it like having a super organized friend who knows exactly where everything

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.880
is on your desk, and can pull out the right folder without you asking twice.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:06.660
The agent works right inside your actual Mac, so we can look at your files, check your

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:10.400
browser, and pull information together into summaries our answers.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:17.360
Most AI tools keep you stuck talking inside their own little window, but this one steps

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:22.420
out and works in the same space where you already do homework or scroll through videos.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:28.060
For students that could mean asking it to gather sources for a paper while you stay in one

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:28.500
place.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:34.780
For anyone making videos or music, it might help sort notes or grab quick facts without

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:35.820
losing your flow.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:42.160
The real shift here is that AI is moving from something you chat with in a box to something

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:45.360
that works alongside you on your real computer.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:52.160
If you have a Mac, head to the Proplexity website or app, find the personal computer feature,

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.260
and try asking it to research a topic you care about right now.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.560
OK, now for my favorite part of the show.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:07.060
We are going to look under the hood at how these AI agents actually decide what to do next.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:12.640
You know how when you plan a group project at school, you do not just stick with one tool

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:13.360
the whole time.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.780
You grab your laptop for research, your phone for quick notes, and maybe a notebook for

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.300
ideas, switching as the task changes.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.020
Imagine an AI doing the exact same thing.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:31.280
When you give it a job on your Mac, it looks at the request and picks the right helper for

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:32.260
each small step.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:38.460
One part might need a web search so it opens the browser like reaching for the right app.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:44.560
Another part might need to read a file on your desktop so it uses a different tool for

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:45.380
that instead.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:52.220
It keeps going, breaking the big task into tiny pieces, and choosing the best digital helper

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:54.880
each time until the whole thing is done.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.720
That is basically what these new AI agents are doing.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.020
They are not magic.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:05.360
They are just really good at splitting requests into steps and matching each step to the

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:05.940
right tool.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.700
And that is basically how AI agents pick tools to get jobs done.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.400
Not so scary once you see the pattern, right?

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.900
Now let's look at some cool stuff you can actually try today.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:26.900
Spotify just added tools that let AI agents build entire podcasts just for you.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:33.240
Instead of listening to the same shows everyone else here, you tell the agent exactly what

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:38.780
you want, like a 10 minute episode about your favorite game or a story that mixes two topics

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:39.300
you love.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.080
It creates the whole thing from scratch.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:48.720
This turns listening from something passive into something you shape yourself, almost like

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.040
directing your own mini radio show.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:57.840
Teens who love niche hobbies or learning random facts will probably enjoy experimenting with

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:58.340
it most.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:06.040
Go to Spotify on your phone, our computer, search for the new AI podcast tools and try prompting

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:11.000
it with something like, make a short podcast about how AI helps artists.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:17.740
You may need a parent's help if you're under 18, but the feature works with regular counts.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:24.480
Another quick thing worth knowing is that you can turn off Google's built-in Gemini AI inside

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.260
Chrome if it feels weird.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:33.520
A small AI model from Google now runs by default in the browser, which surprised people

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.480
and raised privacy questions.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:41.060
The good news is you can remove it in just a few clicks without breaking anything else.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:45.420
This gives you real control over what runs on your own device.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:53.180
Open Chrome, go to Settings, search for Gemini, and follow the steps to disable or uninstall

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:53.800
the model.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:05:00.680
It is a fast way to check exactly what AI features are active and decide what you actually

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:01.420
want running.

